          "title": "You'll want to know: ਗੰਢ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਗੰਢ — gaṇḍh — \"a knot\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਰੱਸੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਇੱਕ ਗੰਢ ਹੈ। rassī vich ikk gaṇḍh hai. There is a knot in the rope."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਗੰਢ (gaṇḍh) is inherited from Sanskrit granthi, \"knot, bunch\"; CDIAL lists Punjabi gaṇḍh, \"knot, joint\" (CDIAL 4354). CDIAL marks the Punjabi row masculine and the Lahnda row feminine; here ਗੰਢ is taught as feminine, as the Lahnda row has it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what you do."
